# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Metric registry — one entry per published metric, Korean and English.
The site builder reads this; nothing about a metric is defined anywhere else.

Fields
  id          column (or table) name in data/derived
  series      A volume · B editions · C sky and weather · D politics · E justice and society
  table       derived CSV the metric lives in
  unit, fmt   display unit and python format spec
  ko / en     name, definition, formula, reading (how to read it), caveat
  reliability how far to trust the number:
                kind = "exact"             counted from the XML; card gives denominator and external check
                       "external-match"    compared with an astronomical computation; card gives the match rate
                       "sampled-precision" keyword hits hand-coded on a stratified sample; card gives precision + CI
              values (rate, ci, n, note) are filled by the metric scripts into data/derived/reliability.json
              and merged at build time — the registry holds the method text only.
"""

